    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d727">

                <pb facs="1058" n="1030" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg1030"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/10–154: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Aldrich</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-10-01T11:00:00+01:00">October 1, 1954—11
                            a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1640. For Lodge from Secretary. Believe your proposal a constructive one and that
                    in connection with dealing with this matter non-member participation, we should
                    make it clear beyond a doubt that on assumption Charter Review Conference is
                    held, we will there propose to remove veto from membership, so that present move
                    only an interim measure which will force hand of Soviet at Review
                        Conference.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d727-f1"/></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aldrich</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
